Hello [~accountid:616fd1373e3753006f97f319] ,

here are the Dovetail”s responses to our specific concerns with the MSA and Terms. Overall, while they cannot change their MSA and Terms for us, they are willing to address our concerns. I hope that this will provide the opportunity to move forward.

*User Terms*

{quote}_Clause 5 section 3 part (iv) states that the service provider is released of any liability related to the quality of the service. This is not acceptable for Bolt and we cannot commit to a service provider that cannot be held accountable for the quality of the service within its reasonable control. Please exclude this part._{quote}

This section relates to the services being unavailable, and does not relate to the quality of the services. To provide comfort to you and your organization, you can track our operational status and uptime [here|https://status.dovetailapp.com/] and [here|https://status.dovetailapp.com/uptime]. 

{quote}_Clause 5 section 4 service provider limits its liability for any breach with 100 dollars. This is not acceptable for Bolt and we cannot commit to a service provider when our possibility to claim any damages is limited unproportionally. Please exclude this sentence._{quote}

These are the User Terms, which relate to the way in which the services are used. Given no fees are payable under the User Terms, this is a proportionate limitation of liability. For completeness, we note that where fees are payable under the MSA (i.e. for Paid Plans), the limitation of liability is proportionate to annual fees payable by the customer. See our comments regarding liability under the MSA below. 

{quote}_Clause 11 (dispute resolution) we cannot agree upon arbitration nor applicable Australian law. Please reword clause 11 and clause 12.7 as follows:_  

_User Terms shall be construed in accordance with and controlled by the laws of England and Wales, without regard to the conflicts of laws provisions thereof, and the parties agree that the competent courts of London, England shall have exclusive jurisdiction to determine all disputes arising out of or relating to these User Terms._{quote}

Dovetail is an Australian-based business and does not do business in the UK. Accordingly, the User Terms are governed by Australian law and we require an Australian venue. We cannot change this on a per-customer basis.

{quote}_Clause 12.7 (jurisdiction) we cannot agree upon applicable Australian law. Please see previous comment._{quote}

See comment above.

*MSA*

{quote}_Clause 13.2 needs change quickly in_ [_tech.world_|http://tech.world/] _and we need to ensure the right to terminate. Thus please add the following sentence to this clause:_

_The Customer may terminate this Agreement or any Order under it for convenience by providing thirty (30) days prior written notice of such termination to Dovetail._{quote}

We don't provide a right for customers to terminate for convenience because our products are offered on a subscription basis and our pricing is based on a fixed minimum term commitment. A right to terminate for convenience undermines this minimum term commitment and is not commercially viable for us.

{quote}_Clause 15.1 and 15.2 will we have a Paid Plan or a Free Plan? If the latter, then (similarly as with the User Terms cl 5 sec 4) please remove limitation of Dovetail’s liability to 100 dollars i.e part (b) in full. This is not acceptable for Bolt and we cannot commit to a service provider when our possibility to claim any damages is limited unproportionally._{quote}

The limitation of liability provisions in our MSA are mutual and help to limit the financial risk exposure of both parties in the unlikely event that something goes wrong. We need to ensure that the agreement is commercially viable for us, so the liability cap referenced is proportionate to the annual fees you pay for your subscription. Whether Bolt is on a Paid Plan or Free Plan is entirely up to Bolt, based on its needs and the plan it selects. Where Bolt has subscribed to a Paid Plan, the limitation of liability will be calculated based on the fees paid by Bolt in the 12 months prior to the liability event.

{quote}_Clause 22 we can accept English law and English courts. Thus please reword as follows:_

_This Agreement shall be construed in accordance with and controlled by the laws of England and Wales, without regard to the conflicts of laws provisions thereof, and the parties agree that the competent courts of London, England shall have exclusive jurisdiction to determine all disputes arising out of or relating to this Agreement._{quote}

As mentioned above, Dovetail is an Australian-based business. However, we have a growing Go-To-Market office in San Francisco as many of our customers are based in the US. Accordingly, we cannot amend the governing law or venue to other jurisdictions.

