Checked bolt-server code and I think found *setnx* [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/geo/route_prediction/main/state/SnappedLocationsBuffer.ts#L27]
So looks like at lease this setnx related keys are located on first node ([route-prediction-westasia1.redis.boltint.net:6379|http://route-prediction-westasia1.redis.boltint.net:6379]).

And it seems that diff in other commands could be related to this as well, since this code has these commands (get, rpush, expire), at least partially

{noformat}    private static readonly PUSH_TO_BUFFER_AND_RETRIEVE_IF_FULL = `
        local created_key = KEYS[1];
        local locations_key = KEYS[2];
        local timestamp = tonumber(ARGV[1]);
        local location = ARGV[2];
        local max_count = tonumber(ARGV[3]);
        local max_age = tonumber(ARGV[4]);
        redis.call('setnx', created_key, timestamp);
        local created = tonumber(redis.call('get', created_key));
        local locations_count = tonumber(redis.call('rpush', locations_key, location));
        redis.call('expire', created_key, 600);
        redis.call('expire', locations_key, 600);
        if locations_count >= max_count or timestamp - created >= max_age then
            local locations = redis.call('lrange', locations_key, 0, -1);
            redis.call('del', locations_key);
            redis.call('del', created_key);
            return locations;
        end
    `;{noformat}

And eval is coming from here {{return (await redis.eval(ctx, SnappedLocationsBuffer.PUSH_TO_BUFFER_AND_RETRIEVE_IF_FULL, keys}} , when this block is executed

